 is always true in a 2-person line, and since videographer is in position 1, Pakistani must be in position 2 (because if Pakistani were in position 1, then Pakistani = videographer, which violates the constraint that they are different people — from constraint 1).\n\nWait — let’s re-express constraint 1:\n\n> \"The person who is Pakistani is on the immediate left or immediate right of the person who is a videographer\"\n\nThis implies they are **different people**, and adjacent. Since there are only two people, they are adjacent by default. So the only way this constraint is meaningful is to say: **Pakistani ≠ videographer**\n\nSo Pakistani cannot be the videographer → So Pakistani is NOT in position 1 → Therefore, Pakistani must be in position 2.\n\nSo:\n- Position 1: Nationality = Nigerian (only one left)\n- Position 2: Nationality = Pakistani\n\nNow let’s summarize everything:\n\n**Position 1:**\n- Job: videographer\n- Movie: thriller\n- Nationality: Nigerian\n\n**Position 2:**\n- Job: freelancer\n- Movie: animation\n- Nationality: Pakistani\n\nNow answer the questions:\n\n1. **What is the job of the person who is Pakistani?**  \n   → Pakistani is in position 2 → Job = freelancer\n\n2. **What is the movie genre of the person who is Pakistani?**  \n   → Position 2 → Movie = animation\n\n3. **What movie genre does the person in position 1 watch?**  \n   → Position 1 → thriller\n\n4. **At what position is the person who is a videographer?**  \n   → Position 1\n\nSo answers in order:\n\n1. freelancer  \n2. animation  \n3. thriller  \n4. 1\n\nFinal answer format: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.12692900002002716}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.023355737328529358}, {"token": " given", "logprob": -0.3868725597858429}, {"token": ":\n\n", "logprob": -0.14301663637161255}, {"token": "-", "logprob": -0.001994288759306073}, {"token":